PATCH 597: the hit reaction a02d keeps its draw across the fire spawn; 459a's verdict exit reports to
the replay.

board:0017.  a02d (the "catch fire" reaction, patch 267) draws once and, when the object has no fire
bits yet, spawns the type-0x1a effect around that draw: `push ax ; mov al,0x1a ; lcall bf3c ; pop ax`
(0x1a045-0x1a04d).  Ghidra took `mov al,0x1a` for the draw's death and set it to 0 after the spawn,
so the first fire on an unlit object always chose the flag LUT's entry 0 (DGROUP:0x964e: bit 1) where
the original draws LUT[rand & 7] -- bit 2 for the type-2 object at 0xc34d at AZER1's step ~1485, the
seeded replay's first differing byte on the full-mission run.

The mission loop's exit on the verdict flag byte[0xe814] (both entries, 459a and 45f7) calls
fist_mission_end_trace(): the replay's three schedules end there and the INT-8s return to the clock,
so the flows after the mission run as they do unscheduled (the port had spun in e4bb's poll wait
with the interrupts still held).

--- a/fist.c
+++ b/fist.c
@@ -14016,6 +14016,7 @@
       while( true ) {
         do {
           if (DAT_2000_a814 != '\0') {
+            { extern void fist_mission_end_trace(void); fist_mission_end_trace(); }   /* PATCH 597: the verdict -- the replay schedules end here (board:0017) */
             FUN_0000_be86();
             FUN_0000_be67();
             return;
@@ -14082,6 +14083,7 @@
       while( true ) {
         do {
           if (DAT_2000_a814 != '\0') {
+            { extern void fist_mission_end_trace(void); fist_mission_end_trace(); }   /* PATCH 597: the verdict -- the replay schedules end here (board:0017) */
             FUN_0000_be86();
             FUN_0000_be67();
             return;
@@ -67215,8 +67217,12 @@
   uVar1 = FUN_0000_b26a();
   if ((DAT_2000_5bd9 == 10) || ((uVar1 & 0x78) == 0)) {
     if ((dg[(unsigned short)(di + 0x19)] & 6) == 0) {
+      /* PATCH 597: `push ax ; mov al,0x1a ; lcall bf3c ; pop ax` (0x1a045-0x1a04d) -- the draw survives
+       * the spawn call; Ghidra's `uVar1 = 0` took `mov al,0x1a` for its death, so the first fire on an
+       * unlit object always chose flag LUT[0] (0x964e: bit 1) where the original draws LUT[rand & 7]
+       * (bit 2 at AZER1's step ~1485 for the type-2 object at 0xc34d -- the seeded replay's first
+       * differing byte on the full-mission run, board:0017). */
       FUN_0000_bf3c(0x1a,param_1,param_2);
-      uVar1 = 0;
     }
     dg[(unsigned short)(di + 0x19)] =
         (unsigned char)(dg[(unsigned short)(di + 0x19)] | dg[(unsigned short)((uVar1 & 7) + 0x964e)]);
